     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Density",
     "md": "**Density = mass ÷ volume**, **ρ = m / V**, so m = ρ × V and V = m / ρ. Units: **g/cm³** or **kg/m³**, with **1 g/cm³ = 1000 kg/m³**. Water has a density of **1.0 g/cm³ (1000 kg/m³)**."
    },
    {
     "type": "illustration",
